astrobench_a877243f10,astrobench_a877243f10_chunk_009,9,Gaia data releases and the 17 th data release from the APOGEE survey with modelsin which eachof our Galaxy’s compo nentsis defined bya DFf(J). The DFsof the stellar and dark haloes were chosen such that these components have nearly isotropic velocity distributionsin orderto avoid the unphysical features describedin Section 2. The new DFs open the wayto producing much more realistic modelsof our Galaxy’s stellar halo andto tightening constraintson the structureof the dark halo. N-body simulationsof the clus teringof dark matter strongly suggest that dark haloes are radially biased. From this fact and the resultsof Section 6 it follows that the dark halo shouldbe quite oblate. Given that,CONCLUSIONS the halo’s contributionto the circular-speed curvevc(R) is,CONCLUSIONS the halo’s contributionto the circular-speed curvevc(R) is,,,,,Distribution functions for spheroids,James Binney,astro-ph.GA,2026-02-26T15:41:51Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2602.23127v1,2602.23127,distribution_functions,140,107,False,False,420,527,True,5.0
