astrobench_3474c47fe1,astrobench_3474c47fe1_chunk_016,16,"and (8). The first and second derivatives are immediately obtained and easily implemented, given the expressions for 𝜌′ 0(𝑟) and 𝜌′′ 0 (𝑟), which are available for the base model. All other intrinsic properties, projected properties, and dynamical properties are automatically calculated using high-order Gauss–Legendre quadrature (for details, see Baesetal. 2021). The additional evaluationof the smoothing function and its derivativesis negligible comparedto the repeated quadrature dominating the evaluationof the dynamical quantities.",2.1 Mathematical formulation,2.1 Mathematical formulation,,,,,Self-consistent dynamical models with a finite extent -- V. Smooth radial truncations and phase-space consistency,Maarten Baes,astro-ph.GA,2026-01-13T09:17:21Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2601.08361v1,2601.08361,distribution_functions,93,71,False,False,840,911,False,2.0
astrobench_3474c47fe1,astrobench_3474c47fe1_chunk_017,17,"feature arises here froman explicitly smooth radial truncation rather than froma sharp cutoffor incomplete mixing, its qualitative structureis similar. This suggests that, despite being phase-space consistent, some softly truncated isotropic models maybe susceptibleto dipole instabilitieson secular timescales. Suchan instability would notin validate the modelsas instantaneous equilibria, butit would imply that they represent metastable configurations whose long-term evo lution may involve slow reorganisationof the central structure. The situation becomes richer for anisotropic distribution functions. Strong radial anisotropyis knownto trigger the radial-orbit instability (Antonov 1973; Hénon 1973; Polyachenko & Shukhman 1981, 2015; Merritt & Aguilar 1985; Barnesetal. 1986), and numerous studies have quantified stability limits for Osipkov–Merritt modelsin termsof the anisotropy radiusor global anisotropy parameters (e.g. Palmer & Papaloizou 1987; Saha 1991; Nipotietal. 2002; Di Cintio & Casetti 2020). In addition, anisotropic spherical systems generically support weakly damped global modes (Weinberg 1991, 1994; Heggieetal. 2020), which canbe destabilisedby relatively small features",2 This intermediate regime mirrors the situation encounteredin the transition,2 This intermediate regime mirrors the situation encounteredin the transition,,,,,Self-consistent dynamical models with a finite extent -- V. Smooth radial truncations and phase-space consistency,Maarten Baes,astro-ph.GA,2026-01-13T09:17:21Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2601.08361v1,2601.08361,distribution_functions,194,149,False,False,1260,1409,False,2.0
