astrobench_1e3dee4300,astrobench_1e3dee4300_chunk_018,18,"DebattistaV. P., LiddicottD. J., KhachaturyantsT., Beraldoe SilvaL., 2020, • Itis possibleto use the conservationof actionto classify the spatial extentof barred regionin simulated galaxies. • The percentage changein action can bea good indicator for stellar orbits that contributeto different morphological featuresin simulated galaxies. While this method, too, has both limitations and advantages, we hope that this work servesto advance ongoing efforts within the fieldto unify the classificationof barsin galaxies and supports future research into bars, the galaxies that host them, and the evolutionof structurein the Universeon the whole.","REFERENCES AbrahamR.G., MerrifieldM.R., EllisR.S., TanvirN.R., BrinchmannJ.,","REFERENCES AbrahamR.G., MerrifieldM.R., EllisR.S., TanvirN.R., BrinchmannJ.,",,,,,Bar Properties and Star-by-Star Bar Membership via Action Conservation,"Elizabeth J. Iles, Finn A. Pal, Joss Bland-Hawthorn, Ken Freeman",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-26T02:45:29Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.24952v1,2603.24952,galactic_dynamics,114,87,False,False,280,367,False,3.0
