astrobench_1e3dee4300,astrobench_1e3dee4300_chunk_026,26,"Bar Properties and Star-by-Star Bar Membership via Action Conservation APPENDIXA: KINEMATIC MAPS & A NSD In Section 3 we notea featurein the action conservation (Figure 3) which mightbe related toa NSD in the centreof the simulated galaxy. Thisis assumed dueto the central feature evidentin the kinematic mapsof this galaxy but has not been subjectedto extensive studyas yet. The relevant kinematic maps (𝑣los, ℎ3) are includedin this appendix for reference. This paper has been typeset froma TEX/LATEX file preparedby the author. Figure A2. The edge-on projected stellar density (upper), mean line-of-sight velocity (𝑣los, middle) and skewness (ℎ3, lower) zoomed-into the centremost (𝑅< 1.5 kpc, 𝑧< 0.6 kpc) regionof the simulated galaxyat the 1 Gyr snapshotto highlight the potential NSD feature.",APPENDIXA: KINEMATIC MAPS & A NSD In Section 3 we notea featurein the action conservation (Figure 3),APPENDIXA: KINEMATIC MAPS & A NSD In Section 3 we notea featurein the action conservation (Figure 3),,,,,Bar Properties and Star-by-Star Bar Membership via Action Conservation,"Elizabeth J. Iles, Finn A. Pal, Joss Bland-Hawthorn, Ken Freeman",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-26T02:45:29Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.24952v1,2603.24952,galactic_dynamics,155,119,False,False,0,119,False,2.0
astrobench_1e3dee4300,astrobench_1e3dee4300_chunk_027,27,"or photometric decomposition (e.g. Reeseetal. 2007; Gadotti 2008; Durbalaetal. 2008, 2009; Weinzirletal. 2009; Kruketal. 2018; Fraser-McKelvieetal. 2025). Visual clas sification (e.g. Nair & Abraham 2010; Hoyleetal. 2011; Mastersetal. 2011, 2012; Melvinetal. 2014; Kruketal. 2018; Mastersetal. 2021; Géronetal. 2021) remains common, as bars are inherently visual features, but thisis increasingly impractical for large surveys andis inherently subjectto significant person-to-person variability (e.g. Lahavetal. 1995; Heidletal. 2013; Qianetal. 2022; Ilesetal. 2025). Crowdsourcing (e.g. Lahavetal. 1995; Fortsonetal.",Bar Properties and Star-by-Star Bar Membership via Action Conservation,Bar Properties and Star-by-Star Bar Membership via Action Conservation,,,,,Bar Properties and Star-by-Star Bar Membership via Action Conservation,"Elizabeth J. Iles, Finn A. Pal, Joss Bland-Hawthorn, Ken Freeman",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-26T02:45:29Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.24952v1,2603.24952,galactic_dynamics,95,73,False,False,420,493,False,1.0
