astrobench_eb380fd57f,astrobench_eb380fd57f_chunk_024,24,"matter halo distortion). We conclude that, when using winding times for physical interpretations: (i) winding times derived from MW phase spirals shouldbe considered lower limits; and (ii) the winding timesin the outer disk are likelytobe more accurate than thosein the inner diskor the Solar Neighborhood. • Disk evolution alone does not providea viableex planation for the slowingof the rateof windingin the inner disk comparedto expectations. This failure suggests significant dynamical effects yettobe explored, suchas the time evolutionof the halo component, the couplingof the halo and disk, and the bulk motionof the disk towards the satelliteas the latter approaches.",7.1.Summary The dynamicsof phase spiral formation and evolution,7.1.Summary The dynamicsof phase spiral formation and evolution,,,,,Phase spirals across galactic disks I: Exploring dynamical influences on winding,"Kiyan Tavangar, Kathryn V. Johnston, Jason A. S. Hunt, Axel Widmark, Chris Hamilton, Michael S. Petersen, Martin D. Weinberg",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-24T18:00:00Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.23588v1,2603.23588,galactic_dynamics,128,98,False,False,140,238,True,4.0
