astrobench_d82fccf1ca,astrobench_d82fccf1ca_chunk_008,8,"momentum. The chemical evolutionof the starsis treatedin the same wayasin the fiducial Auriga simulation. Re-simulatinga halo using the Superstars method keeps galaxy prop erties largely preserved, with variations falling within the rangeof intrinsic variations found among realisations run ona differentma chineor witha different random number seed (Pakmoretal. 2025b). The changes thatdo occur are smaller than the systematic shifts causedby changing the mass resolutionof the gas. For more detailson the method, we refer the readerto Pakmoretal. (2025a). 2.1.1 Halo 18 In this studywe use halo 18 from the fiducial Auriga suiteof sim ulations, re-simulated using the Superstars method. The simulation",2.1 Auriga Superstars Milky Way analogue The simulated galaxywe explorein this workis partof the newly,2.1 Auriga Superstars Milky Way analogue The simulated galaxywe explorein this workis partof the newly,,,,,Stirring Things Up: Bar-induced substructures in the stellar halo of a cosmological Milky Way analogue,"Thomas Tomlinson, Francesca Fragkoudi, Andreia Carrillo, Azadeh Fattahi, Paula Gherghinescu, Alis Deason, Rüdiger Pakmor, Robert J. J. Grand, Facundo A. Gómez, Freeke van de Voort, Rebekka Bieri",astro-ph.GA,2026-01-20T19:14:36Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2601.14409v1,2601.14409,galactic_dynamics,129,99,False,False,980,1079,False,3.0
astrobench_d82fccf1ca,astrobench_d82fccf1ca_chunk_009,9,"Stirring Things Up: Bar-induced substructures in the stellar halo of a cosmological Milky Way analogue 1 We note that the simulation studied here usesa variationof the Superstars method, witha factorof ∼2 larger kickto the birth velocityto stars. However, we highlight that this does not havea significant impacton the propertiesof the galaxy – see the discussion and AppendixA in Pakmoretal. 2025a for more details. resonances, we takea bar pattern speedof 25.1 rad Gyr−1, whichis obtainedby performingan FFT on the phaseof the bar. Merger Peak stellar mass (𝑀⊙) Peak halo mass (𝑀⊙) Accreted fraction Mean [Fe/H] Infall time (Gyrs) Infall red shift M1 1.5×108 3.0 × 109 0.1 -1.16 12.52 4.6 M2 1.9×108 9.6 × 109 0.1 -1.18 12.11 3.7 M3 5.6×108 1.6 × 1010 0.12 -0.89 9.47 1.5 M4 1.5×109 3.6 × 1010 0.61 -0.63 9.29 1.4",1 We note that the simulation studied here usesa variationof the Superstars,1 We note that the simulation studied here usesa variationof the Superstars,,,,,Stirring Things Up: Bar-induced substructures in the stellar halo of a cosmological Milky Way analogue,"Thomas Tomlinson, Francesca Fragkoudi, Andreia Carrillo, Azadeh Fattahi, Paula Gherghinescu, Alis Deason, Rüdiger Pakmor, Robert J. J. Grand, Facundo A. Gómez, Freeke van de Voort, Rebekka Bieri",astro-ph.GA,2026-01-20T19:14:36Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2601.14409v1,2601.14409,galactic_dynamics,177,136,False,False,0,136,False,3.0
